  "query_preview": "..\nIsolated showers and thunderstorms tonight are expected to become\nmore scattered for Guam and Rota tonight, though more so over the\ncoastal waters than on land. This pattern should remain through\ntomorrow morning before daytime heating and light winds allow for\nscattered island effect showers and isolated thunderstorms to \ndevelop over Tinian and Saipan. These island effect storms will also\nbe possible Thursday for Tinian and Saipan. Winds appear likely to \nremain just high enough for any island effect over Guam to stay \noffshore. However, scattered monsoonal showers and isolated \nthunderstorms will remain possible. This monsoon flow is expected to \nslowly drift north throughout the week, bringing slightly higher\nwinds and moisture to the Marianas as soon as Thursday night. Locally\nheavy showers will be possible as well but the flood risk remains\nlow. This monsoon pattern may then continue for the rest of the\nforecast period.",
